From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HFM <hfm@example.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 10:40:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] subsys/pmci/pldm: add DSP0248 Type 2 (Platform
 Monitoring) responder

Extend the PLDM subsystem with a DMTF DSP0248 Type 2 responder so a
management controller (e.g. OpenBMC's pldmd platform-mc) can discover a
sensor terminus and poll it.

Key pieces:

  * include/zephyr/pmci/pldm/pldm_platform.h - public API:
      pldm_platform_add_numeric_sensor(), pldm_platform_responder_register().

  * subsys/pmci/pldm/pldm_platform.c - Type 2 responder.
      Serves a compile-time PDR repository (one Terminus Locator PDR plus
      one Numeric Sensor PDR per registered sensor) through
      GetPDRRepositoryInfo (0x50) / GetPDR (0x51); GetSensorReading (0x11)
      returns live values via each sensor's read callback;
      GetStateSensorReadings and PlatformEventMessage are handled minimally.
      Encode/decode is delegated to openbmc/libpldm.

  * subsys/pmci/pldm/pldm_base.c - discovery plumbing.
      pldm_base_register_type() lets a non-base type register its version
      and command bitmap so the Type 0 discovery commands (GetPLDMTypes /
      GetPLDMVersion / GetPLDMCommands) advertise it. The Type 2 responder
      calls this at registration time.

  * subsys/pmci/pldm/pldm.c - ISR-safety fix.
      The requester slot lock is delivered from libmctp's RX path, which
      can run in interrupt context, so req_lock is switched from k_mutex to
      k_spinlock (a mutex may not be locked in an ISR).

  * Kconfig: CONFIG_PLDM_TYPE_PLATFORM (selects REQUIRES_STD_C11 for the
    libpldm platform encoders) and CONFIG_PLDM_PLATFORM_MAX_SENSORS.

Signed-off-by: HFM <hfm@example.com>
